<http://data.silknow.org/event/2ec0fa1a-1592-39be-857a-38e27d5b86ad>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "the programme gives the names of the author of <i>Currupt Practices</i> -  F.A. Marshall, and its cast - Mr. Coglan, Mrs, George Vincent, Mr. G.F. Neville, Mr. F. Stainforth, Mr. E. Selwyn, Mr. Edwards, Miss Fitz-Inman, Miss Louisa Thorne, Miss L. Wilson, Miss Graham, Miss Susan Rignold. <i>Chilpéric</i> was adapted into English by Messrs. R. Reece, F.A. Marshall and R. Mansell, and the cast comprised Mons. Hervé, Mr. Coglan, Mr. Farquharson, Mons. Marius, Mr. Angyalfi, Mr. Geo. Vincent, Mr. J. Odell, Miss Nellie Nesbit, Miss Emily Muir, Selena Dolaro, Louisa Thorne, Miss Romanelli, Miss Graham, Miss Lovell, Miss Rignold, Miss L. Wilson, Miss A. Lee, Miss A. Egerton, Miss Lily Bell, and Miss B. Linden. Mr. F. Musgrave was the conductor. The Stage Director was Mr. R. Mansell, the ASM Mr. J. Milano, and the Acting Manager Mr. T. Roberts."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/234ca1e5-40a5-34f0-8297-91eb56ca7ae2> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Gabrielle Enthoven Collection" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/fb70d4db-29ff-3b22-9589-9f2c1e7491ff> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "the programme gives the names of the author of <i>Currupt Practices</i> -  F.A. Marshall, and its cast - Mr. Coglan, Mrs, George Vincent, Mr. G.F. Neville, Mr. F. Stainforth, Mr. E. Selwyn, Mr. Edwards, Miss Fitz-Inman, Miss Louisa Thorne, Miss L. Wilson, Miss Graham, Miss Susan Rignold. <i>Chilpéric</i> was adapted into English by Messrs. R. Reece, F.A. Marshall and R. Mansell, and the cast comprised Mons. Hervé, Mr. Coglan, Mr. Farquharson, Mons. Marius, Mr. Angyalfi, Mr. Geo. Vincent, Mr. J. Odell, Miss Nellie Nesbit, Miss Emily Muir, Selena Dolaro, Louisa Thorne, Miss Romanelli, Miss Graham, Miss Lovell, Miss Rignold, Miss L. Wilson, Miss A. Lee, Miss A. Egerton, Miss Lily Bell, and Miss B. Linden. Mr. F. Musgrave was the conductor. The Stage Director was Mr. R. Mansell, the ASM Mr. J. Milano, and the Acting Manager Mr. T. Roberts."@en .

